# BOOLEAN: Difference A - B of a 100 cm Box and a radius-50 Sphere sunk into its top corner leaves a spherical bite; Undo brings both inputs back
# Ours applies Boolean at once (no preview session, unlike UE UCSGMeshesTool): its "Cancel" is the one undo step it records.
Дано run Panel "Open Modeling"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 230,260,300
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.5,-0.45,-0.74
Дано --subject modeling set CreateShape.Box.Width 100
Дано --subject modeling set CreateShape.Box.Depth 100
Дано --subject modeling set CreateShape.Box.Height 100
Дано run Modeling "Create shape tool: Box"
Дано run Modeling "Create shape: place at the viewport centre"
Дано --subject selection set Translation 0,0,0
Дано --subject modeling set CreateShape.Sphere.Radius 50
Дано run Modeling "Create shape tool: Sphere"
Дано run Modeling "Create shape: place at the viewport centre"
Дано --subject selection set Translation 40,60,40
Дано run Modeling "Active tool: Accept"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 150,190,180
Дано run Entity Box
Дано run Entity "Add to selection Sphere"
Дано run Modeling "Boolean operation: Difference A - B"
Дано run Modeling "Boolean write to: Input"
Дано run Modeling "Boolean inputs: Delete Inputs"
Тогда-вид 0_inputs the Box with the Sphere sunk into its near top corner
Когда run Modeling "Boolean tool: Boolean"
Тогда 1_difference the Box has a smooth spherical bite cut out of its near top corner; the Sphere is gone from viewport and Outliner
Когда run Action Undo
Тогда 2_undo the Box is whole again and the Sphere is back in its corner; Outliner lists both
